            <div xml:id="d118-a1-a3">

                <pb facs="0362" n="304" sameAs="frus:frus1866p3/pg304"/>


                <opener><dateline rendition="#center">[From La
                            Sociedad—<placeName>Mexico</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1866-08-28">August 28, 1866</date>.]</dateline></opener>
                <head>Treasury division.</head>
                <p>The following was published in Zacatecas:</p>
                <p rendition="#center">DEPARTMENT OF FINANCE—MILITARY SUB-INTENDANCY—TREASURY
                    INSPECTOR OF THE STATE OF GUANAJUATO.</p>
                <p rendition="#right"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Leon, August</hi> 2, 1866.</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">To the Citizen Prefect:</hi></p>
                <p>The military intendant, Mr. Friant, appointed minister of finance, charges me to
                    send you the following despatch, which was received by telegraph:</p>
                <p>“The minister of finance gives full power to sub-intendants or officers to
                    perform the duties of sub-intendants, inspectors, and controllers in all the
                    offices of finance, each in his respective department. The prefects will
                    accredit these officers to the chief of the bureau.</p>
                <p rendition="#right">“FRIANT, <hi rendition="#italic">Minister of
                    Finance</hi>.”</p>
                <p>Accept, Mr. Prefect, the assurances of my high consideration.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>DAMARTIUS, <hi rendition="#italic">Military Sub-inspector of the
                            Treasury in the Department of Guanajuita.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
